# ── Benchmarks (benchmarks/) ──────────────────────────────────
# AppWorld's data and anything derived from a run. This is a
# licence constraint, not housekeeping: `benchmarks/data/LICENSE`
# says the protected portion is released encrypted and that "any
# public redistribution of it (or of its derivatives) must also be
# done in an encrypted format". This repository is public, and the
# project embeds a canary string to detect the benchmark leaking
# into training corpora.
#
# `experiments/` is derivative — every task's environment_io.md
# carries their API documentation and task content verbatim.
# Together these are ~294MB that `git check-ignore` confirmed were
# not covered by anything above.
#
# The encrypted leaderboard.bundle is the one shareable artifact,
# and it belongs in a PR to appworld-leaderboard rather than here.
benchmarks/data/
benchmarks/experiments/
benchmarks/**/leaderboard.bundle
